  "text:1200000001:1": {
   "parse": {
    "title": "The Lantern Keeper",
    "pageid": 0,
    "revid": 1200000001,
    "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Plot\">Plot</h2></div><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1\">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}</style><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/X\">Lantern Keeper (novel)</a></div><figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Lighthouse.jpg\"><img src=\"//upload.example/l.jpg\"></a><figcaption>The fictional lighthouse used as a set</figcaption></figure><p>On a windswept island off a fictional northern coast, Edda Morn, a retired ferry pilot, keeps an old lighthouse running long after the shipping lane has closed.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\">[1]</a></sup> Her only company is a radio that picks up distant fishing boats. One night the lamp fails, and a small boat carrying a runaway teenager named Pim runs aground on the rocks below.</p>\n<p>Edda reluctantly takes Pim in while the storm season closes the crossing. Pim claims to be fleeing an uncle, but letters hidden in the boat suggest a different story, and Edda begins to question the child&#39;s account.<sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\">[<i><a href=\"/wiki/W:CN\">citation needed</a></i>]</sup> Together they repair the lamp, trade stories and argue about whether the light is still worth keeping.</p>\n<p>When a coast guard cutter arrives with news of a missing heir, Edda must decide whether to hand Pim over or help the child escape across the strait. She chooses to sail Pim to the mainland herself, losing the lighthouse keys in the crossing. In the final scene, years later, a grown Pim returns to the island and relights the lamp for a new keeper, while the old radio crackles with a familiar voice that seems to thank them both for coming home.</p></div>"
   }
  },
