  "text:1000000003:1": {
   "parse": {
    "title": "Harbor Lights (TV series)",
    "pageid": 0,
    "revid": 1000000003,
    "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Premise\">Premise</h2></div><p>A disgraced harbor pilot returns to her fictional hometown to run the family tugboat company and finds the town divided over a new container port.</p></div>"
   }
  },
  "text:1000000003:3": {
   "parse": {
    "title": "Harbor Lights (TV series)",
    "pageid": 0,
    "revid": 1000000003,
    "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Series_overview\">Series overview</h2></div><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/L\">List of Harbor Lights episodes</a></div><table class=\"wikitable plainrowheaders\"><tbody><tr><th>Season</th><th>Episodes</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>10</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
   }
  },
  "text:1000000003:4": {
   "parse": {
    "title": "Harbor Lights (TV series)",
    "pageid": 0,
    "revid": 1000000003,
    "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Season_synopses\">Season synopses</h2></div><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Season_1_(2013)\">Season 1 (2013)</h3></div><p>Nora Quill comes back to Port Adley after losing her pilot&#39;s license and takes over the struggling tugboat firm her late father left to her and her younger brother Cal. The town council is about to approve a container port that would save the local economy but drown the old fishing quarter. Nora signs on as the port&#39;s chief pilot, which alienates Cal and the fishing families who raised her.<sup class=\"reference\">[3]</sup></p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Season_2_(2014)\">Season 2 (2014)</h3></div><p>A collision in the new channel kills a deckhand, and an inquiry blames the tug crew. Nora suspects the port company falsified the depth surveys. She and Cal reconcile to gather evidence, helped by a retired surveyor and a local reporter, while the company tries to buy the tugboat firm out from under them.</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Seasons_3–5_(2015–2018)\">Seasons 3–5 (2015–2018)</h3></div><p>The later seasons follow the fallout of the inquiry across the whole town. The fishing quarter organizes, the port changes owners twice, and Nora is forced to choose between her license and her brother&#39;s freedom. The series ends with the firm sold, Cal released, and Nora piloting the last ship out of the old harbor before it closes for good, watched by the families who once turned their backs on her.</p></div>"
   }
  },
